From: our reconstruction of GL.iNet's 4.6.x MPTCP backport
Subject: [PATCH] mptcp: report subflow priority changes from the receive path

In GL.iNet's 4.6.2-4.6.8 kernels mptcp_rcv_space_adjust() (inlined into
mptcp_recvmsg) still calls mptcp_event(MPTCP_EVENT_SUB_PRIORITY, ...) when
is_set_backup_for_rx() marks a subflow; their later backport (ours, and
GL.iNet's 4.7.0+ kernels) has the call commented out. With it active,
mptcp_recvmsg is GL.iNet's 4.6.2 function instruction for instruction
(578 instructions; single-object compile validated against our vmlinux).

---
--- a/net/mptcp/protocol.c
+++ b/net/mptcp/protocol.c
@@ -1964,7 +1964,7 @@
 
 		if (is_set_backup_for_rx(subflow, rcv_max, tp->bytes_received,
 		   tp->rcv_rtt_est.rtt_us, gl_ratio) == 1) {
-			//mptcp_event(MPTCP_EVENT_SUB_PRIORITY, mptcp_sk(subflow->conn), mptcp_subflow_tcp_sock(subflow), GFP_ATOMIC);
+			mptcp_event(MPTCP_EVENT_SUB_PRIORITY, mptcp_sk(subflow->conn), mptcp_subflow_tcp_sock(subflow), GFP_ATOMIC);
 		}
 	}
 
